# Default-deny. The build context is exactly what the image needs and nothing
# else, so nothing new at the repository root — history, tests, editor state,
# local tooling directories, a stray .env — can leak into an image or bust the
# build cache by changing. Anything the Dockerfile needs is re-included below.
*

!global.json
!src/

# Build output, in case the context is a working checkout that has been built
# locally: it would otherwise be copied over the layer the SDK just produced.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Local developer settings and per-environment overrides never belong in an
# image; configuration arrives as environment variables at run time.
**/*.user
**/appsettings.*.local.json
**/Properties/launchSettings.json
